# Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# ── Kit (formerly ConvertKit) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these two and newsletter signups are added straight to your Kit form,
# which then sends the confirmation email and runs whatever sequence you have
# attached. This is the destination that actually subscribes people.
#
# API key:  Kit → Settings → Developer → API Keys → "V4 API key"
# Form ID:  open the form in Kit; it is the number in the URL
#           (app.kit.com/forms/designers/1234567/edit → 1234567)
KIT_API_KEY=your-kit-v4-api-key
KIT_FORM_ID=1234567

# ── Supabase (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A second copy of the list, under your own control. Leave unset and signups
# append to data/subscribers.jsonl instead (local only).
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Data API for the URL,
# and → API Keys for the service role key.
#
# The service role key bypasses row-level security. It is only ever read in
# app/api/subscribe/route.ts, which runs on the server. Never expose it to the
# browser and never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Optional, defaults to "subscribers"
# SUPABASE_SUBSCRIBERS_TABLE=subscribers
